      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "HUANG Shao-chi 黃紹箕 (T. 仲弢, H. 鮮庵), 1854–1908, Jan., official and educationalist, a native of Jui-an, Chekiang, was a son of Huang T'i-fang [q. v.]. In youth he studied Sung philosophy and the methods of the School of Han Learning (see under Ku Yen-wu), but later was much influenced by the pragmatic ideas of Chang Chih-tung [q. v.].",
